   "title": "About this workflow",
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "# Dub · LipDub / DubIt (LTX-2.3)\n\nYour take is the IC-LoRA reference (downscale 1). Its audio only conditions the **voice**; new speech in the target language is generated from the prompt, with matching lips.\n\n- Models: LTX-2.3 22B dev fp8 + distilled 1.1 LoRA (0.5) + LipDub IC-LoRA 0.9 (1.0), Gemma 3 12B fp4 text encoder, x2 spatial upscaler\n- Stage 1 at half resolution (8 sigmas), latent x2 upscale, stage 2 at 704×1280 (3 sigmas, stage-1 speech frozen)\n\n| App input | API node.input |\n|---|---|\n| `video` | `7.file` |\n| `prompt` | `11.text` |\n| `seed` | `24.noise_seed`, `50.noise_seed` |\n| `lat_w` | `14.width` |\n| `lat_h` | `14.height` |\n| `frames` | `14.length`, `31.frames_number` |\n\n**Nodes in yellow are the ones the app sets on every job** (see `dub_bindings.json`); every other value is exactly what the app submits. Each node keeps its API id in Properties → `api_id`.\n\nThis is a view of `workflows/dub_api.json` (what the app sends to Comfy Cloud). All models are open weights; file names and download links: `workflows/README.md`."
   ],
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
